{"title":"2007 USA TST Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4d82b157094a623cf465e56ea889ad41edcf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e76cd239b6f2565d2817410edc5cbd49a4508a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are chords of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4d82b157094a623cf465e56ea889ad41edcf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e76cd239b6f2565d2817410edc5cbd49a4508a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and on ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.  Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  Let the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e76cd239b6f2565d2817410edc5cbd49a4508a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4d82b157094a623cf465e56ea889ad41edcf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />.  Prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d297cc23b920d457aaf7aad17f496504a40580b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q, X, Y, Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 USA TST Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59a8a111d699794e03e450527ae6b004cb3d31f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}\\le a_{2}\\le ...\\le a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66ad86d8ed4009a69e25c98230a1a84d3ba3bb50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{1}\\le b_{2}\\le ... \\le b_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> be two nonincreasing sequences of reals such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b47c460372dc535a674795356bbf2b64d86647f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}\\le b_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4022cf84211cc0c1b0d86f74e45e682b0e3f4315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}+a_{2}\\le b_{1}+b_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb525b2d736463cf0d1b97df8bd1602a84248d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3791ae449f1eb76ea10cd1a92626a38079e2be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle a_{1}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{n-1}\\le b_{1}+b_{2}+\\ldots+b_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"336\" height=\"18\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0ef2a6e87df9f3df8496bde443cd8644e32f51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle a_{1}+a_{2}+\\ldots+a_{n}=b_{1}+b_{2}+\\ldots+b_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"299\" height=\"15\" />\nFor any real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, the number of pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811480f547c16afc74ffca555e4fd6c166ccfa68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bca8bcb9b950d4db4bf687a7af9f571abd03ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}-a_{j}=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to the number of pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b7219b4e846cc130222d0f286c2444bf404140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k, l)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf01f5ede47a987e687209a3e007e6b7f7cee219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k}-b_{l}=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/9/d89b273ce0a5f03108709a8b3dd63c590a306b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}=b_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c91591e92f627ad57ae7ce0e12631b8db78b42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1, 2, ..., n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 USA TST Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d0782147d49f0c8557eae3b13b4bd2bd3adc8565.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\in (0, \\frac{\\pi}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"76\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48704959b0de00c1daac5fdb467a4a3842d65924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle  \\cos{\\theta}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is irrational.  If, for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/8002a43ee1ea75697ce7e7da3d6bff7232aaefe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos{(k\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a650196e6ba59928d16eaf181f4acd89f3a6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\cos{([k+1]\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> are both rational, then show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/40448f6970d277745d3544863f7007df728816b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 USA TST Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Are there two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> such that, for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8eff60a04285cc6790889a0d6663945c9c426b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{n}-n$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 USA TST Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  Let the perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5b93dbd5e47d3865c56f03ec1213bb82256a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AT$\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> meet ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a32b756c9cc2f727157bce98455453d2daf14057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{1}, C_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9988fbe7f7b42a0b56481882dfc4e08246d9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ST$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1edb83de21343022a71923f186ab340e25a475a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{1}T=C_{1}T=BT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" /> and so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/97531e1861626687838b2e7ff029fc9d18c69871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/070c7d87bd9292aca425a5c4baf16e445b195def.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AB_{1}C_{1}}\\sim \\triangle{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 USA TST Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047b12a11328c03bc0c89a79615dcdc3bcb5bde8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r(2i-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> be the remainder mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c2fa23f6d345eb6b967ae9416712eaecf7741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> from 0 to 1023, inclusive, of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/92766f943f8656d021fd60a91b840665c77a3913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2i-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47455efaba500c9e019bb068db7bf079f4180bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1, 2, ..., 512$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />.  Call the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/ceef0566a45359124fb751b5f57d292d1747ce31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{r(1),\\ r(3),\\ r(5),\\ ...,\\ r(1023)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" /> the <i>remainder sequence</i> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Call a remaidner sequence <b>complete</b> if it is a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b1a3795acb9ed2326188c6c31659d48aed4e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 3, 5, ..., 1023\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />.  Show that the number of complete remainder sequences is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a9ab6f3e90a52a13847a0e58d090e949ff72a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{35}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2007 USA TST Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_USA_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=TST\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"TST\">TST</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018053602\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced exp